reference[27]: Reclaim one lease only when its owner is proven dead on this machine. Preview by,"default. --confirm destroys the resource, verifies it is gone, then forgets the",lease. An alive owner is refused (owner_alive) even after expiry; unknown,liveness is refused (owner_unknown). Expiry-driven reclaim stays with sweep.,"A lease already gone is status already_done. Statuses: preview, reclaimed,",already_done.,"Examples:","  dibs reclaim <id>","  dibs reclaim <id> --confirm","Output: --axi for agents, --json for scripts (mutually exclusive).","Default: human on terminals; AXI for pipes or DIBS_AXI=1.","Lease commands: --full restores complete AXI records/text; JSON is always complete.","","Contract 1 (reconcile, reclaim, explain, extend, release, and --pending/--key):","exit 0 success with status; 1 operation failed, records retained; 2 usage;","3 refused, nothing changed, with a stable reason: not_found, wrong_machine,","not_pending, already_leased, key_conflict, handle_exists, handle_mismatch,","resource_absent, ambiguous, owner_alive, owner_unknown, expired, owner_dead,","job_deadline. Output carries contract: 1. See docs/consumer-contract.md.","","Exit codes: 0 success (including no-ops), 1 operation failed, 2 invalid usage.","dibs job: child's exit code on completion; 124 deadline killed child;",75 (EX_TEMPFAIL) no slot within wait. Dibs's own 1/2 apply only when no child,was started. Signal termination returns 128 + signal number. Helper/wait,failures after start use 125/126 and diagnostics on stderr.,76 is SSH transport/protocol failure with unknown remote result (stderr).,Child exit 255 is preserved and is not confused with SSH failure.
usage: "dibs reclaim <id> [--confirm] [--axi | --json]"
